10
00:50:57,142 --> 00:51:03,142
The Quick and the Dead is a 1995 American revisionist
Western film directed by Sam Raimi.

11
00:56:02,857 --> 00:56:08,857
The film stars Sharon Stone, Gene Hackman, Russell Crowe, and Leonardo DiCaprio.

12
01:01:08,571 --> 01:01:14,571
The screenplay was written by Simon Moore, but
includes contributions from Joss Whedon.

13
01:06:14,285 --> 01:06:20,285
The story focuses on "The Lady" (Stone), a gunfighter who rides into the
frontier town of Redemption, controlled by John Herod (Hackman).

14
01:11:20,000 --> 01:11:26,000
The Lady joins a deadly dueling competition in an attempt
to exact revenge for her father's death.

15
01:16:25,714 --> 01:16:31,714
Simon Moore's script was purchased by Sony Pictures Entertainment in May 1993,
and actress Sharon Stone signed on as both star and co-producer.

16
01:21:31,428 --> 01:21:37,428
Development was fast tracked after director Sam Raimi's hiring, and principal
photography began in Old Tucson Studios in Arizona on November 21, 1993.

17
01:26:37,142 --> 01:26:43,142
The film was distributed by TriStar Pictures and was released in the United States on February 10,
1995, to a dismal box-office performance, receiving mixed reviews from critics.

18
01:31:42,857 --> 01:31:48,857
In later years, however, the film has earned critical praise, especially for the performances, direction,
cinematography, and musical score, with some critics noting it as underrated in Raimi's catalog.

19
01:36:48,571 --> 01:36:54,571
The film explores themes of gunslinger, revenge, prairie, shootout, awestruck.

20
01:41:54,285 --> 01:42:00,285
The tone is emotional and intense.
